# Cloudflare Pages redirects. This file is copied verbatim to the site root by
# the Eleventy passthrough (src/static -> "."), so it lands at _site/_redirects
# where Pages reads it.
#
# The Stripe checkout/portal edge functions in openshore.code.ai
# (supabase/functions/stripe-checkout) default their success/cancel/portal
# return URLs to https://openshore.ai/os-code/ (?checkout=success on success),
# a holdover from when this page lived at openshore.ai/os-code/ on the
# Open-Shore-LLC-Homepage site. Now that OpenShore is the whole site at the
# root, keep that path alive as a redirect rather than editing and redeploying
# a live payments function; Cloudflare Pages forwards the query string, so
# ?checkout=success still reaches the page.
# Since 2026-11-07 the root is the web app, so it lands on the site's home,
# /about/, which still carries the checkout runtime.
/os-code/  /about/  301

# openshore.ai is the web app (founder, 2026-11-07, "like Claude.ai does"), and
# this site moved under /about/. Every page it had at the root keeps working:
# links on the web, the app builds already installed (Settings' Privacy and
# Terms rows), and App Store Connect's privacy and support URLs all 301 to the
# page's new home. The root itself is NOT redirected: it is the app.
/llm-choice/      /about/llm-choice/      301
/llm-choice       /about/llm-choice/      301
/privacy/         /about/privacy/         301
/privacy          /about/privacy/         301
/terms/           /about/terms/           301
/terms            /about/terms/           301
/ethics/          /about/ethics/          301
/ethics           /about/ethics/          301
/sustainability/  /about/sustainability/  301
/sustainability   /about/sustainability/  301
/self-hosting/    /about/self-hosting/    301
/self-hosting     /about/self-hosting/    301
/support/         /about/support/         301
/support          /about/support/         301
